 "about_text": "Q Pop is a small shop and gallery in the historic Little Tokyo district of downtown Los Angeles, opened on November 12, 2010 by co-owners Chris Mitchell, an animation production designer, and Miki Panteepo, a former model turned businesswoman. The shop specializes in curated artist-made goods, vinyl toys, rare records, and designer T-shirts, and is the exclusive West Coast seller of Japanese artist Konatsu. Alongside retail, Q Pop houses a mini gallery space that regularly hosts exhibitions, events, and performances featuring illustration and animation talent from studios such as Disney, Nickelodeon, Cartoon Network, Sony, Warner Brothers, and Netflix.",
